(7761022, 1285496, 127617, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by noraneko:</b></div><hr/><i> What a great capture! My pick for the blue, good luck! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Catherine for your vote of confidence! Much appreciated! <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-12-14 19:17:06.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by noraneko: What a great capture! My pick for the blue, good luck!   Thank you Catherine for your vote of confidence! Much appreciated! ', '2023-12-14 18:09:49.000000', '2023-12-14 19:17:06.000000', 0),
(7761025, 1285496, 127617, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by spencelg:</b></div><hr/><i> Lol! Tug-of-war! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, they were at a stand-off for a little bit, before it got a little wild.</td>', 'Originally posted by spencelg: Lol! Tug-of-war!   Yes, they were at a stand-off for a little bit, before it got a little wild.', '2023-12-14 18:12:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7761026, 1285496, 127617, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> Well captured. Who won? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Marion! The one on the right ended up with the fish and later grabbed the other great blue heron by it''s head and submitted his fellow heron. I stepped in, and broke them apart, once that happened to make sure there were no major injuries. The one on the right already had an injured wing. We called some wild life rescuers about it a couple of times (two days in a row), and I hope they eventually came to help him out.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-12-14 18:17:52.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jomari: Well captured. Who won?   Thank you Marion! The one on the right ended up with the fish and later grabbed the other great blue heron by it''s head and submitted his fellow heron. I stepped in, and broke them apart, once that happened to make sure there were no major injuries. The one on the right already had an injured wing. We called some wild life rescuers about it a couple of times (two days in a row), and I hope they eventually came to help him out.', '2023-12-14 18:17:10.000000', '2023-12-14 18:17:52.000000', 0),
(7761027, 1285496, 127617, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> INCREDIBLE ..!!..<br/>national geographic worthy .. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Roz, that means a LOT, especially coming from YOU! Love your photography in general and you macro stuff in particular. Never short of stunning, and Award Worthy!!</td>', 'Originally posted by roz: INCREDIBLE ..!!..national geographic worthy .. :)   Thanks Roz, that means a LOT, especially coming from YOU! Love your photography in general and you macro stuff in particular. Never short of stunning, and Award Worthy!!', '2023-12-14 19:13:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7761028, 1285496, 127617, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by digifotojo:</b></div><hr/><i> Gave this a 10.. amazing capture! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh my Joanna! Blushing! Thank you!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-12-14 19:15:17.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by digifotojo: Gave this a 10.. amazing capture!   Oh my Joanna! Blushing! Thank you!', '2023-12-14 19:14:36.000000', '2023-12-14 19:15:17.000000', 0),
